Check your understanding here. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 5, 10, 15, 18, 22, 23, 25, 30};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 10) return steps; if (a[mid] < 10) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

Think through this worked case. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {4, 7, 4, -4, 2, 5, 3, -3};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i += 2) acc += a[i];
return acc;

At a planning meeting, a researcher summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What does this string routine return?
String s = "ecbci";
int acc = 0, target = 'a';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

In a lab report, a researcher summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Here is a question to solve. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {4, 7, 9, 13, 17, 21, 25};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 38) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 38) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

During a field test, a researcher summarizes the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(5);
Node b = new Node(35);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

The case below gives the figures. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {7, 8, 11, 13, 17, 19, 20, 23, 28, 29};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 34) return steps; if (a[mid] < 34) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps; Which answer is correct for this case?

